  "recipes.reserve-ip.cta": "Go to DHCP",
  "recipes.reserve-ip.step1": "In *Hosts*, find the device and copy its *MAC* (the network card's own ID number).",
  "recipes.reserve-ip.step2": "Open the *DHCP* screen and go to *Reservations*.",
  "recipes.reserve-ip.step3": "Enter the *MAC*, the *fixed IP* you want and a name, then save.",
  "recipes.reserve-ip.step4": "Click *Apply*. The device picks up that IP the next time it connects.",
  "recipes.port-forward.title": "Open / forward a port",
  "recipes.port-forward.summary": "Let something outside reach a service of yours (server, camera, game).",
  "recipes.port-forward.cta": "Go to Firewall",
  "recipes.port-forward.step1": "Reserve a *fixed IP* for the device in *DHCP*, so the forward never ends up pointing at some other machine.",
  "recipes.port-forward.step2": "Open *Firewall → Port forwarding*.",
  "recipes.port-forward.step3": "Enter the *external port*, the *protocol* (TCP/UDP) and the device's *internal IP:port*, then save.",
  "recipes.port-forward.step4": "Open only what you actually need — every open port is a way into your network.",
  "recipes.block-device.title": "Block a device from the network",
